; generated-format instantiation 2026-08-08; re-carved per [[DECISIONS#d11-universal-path|D11 universal-path]] same day —
; the concept was mis-attached as "universal location"; the old designation
; itself committed the path/location conflation its own segment diagnoses.
|term[universal-path]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss A path whose origin is universal — routable to the destination from any origin (within a bounded context); synonym: absolute path.
  :see-also [@origin @path]
  |designation universal-path
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |designation absolute-path
    :status admitted
    :channel prose
  ; hidden = resolvable in search/lint, never suggested — exactly this case:
  ; the pre-D11 designation, kept findable because the corpus wrote it for a day.
  |designation universal-location
    :status hidden
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-locations-and-paths
    :anchor universal-location
    :projection paraphrase
    A path that can be used effectively from anywhere — its components progressively resolve from any origin to the destination; equivalently, a path with a universal origin.
  |set-rel :kind subset-of :to @path
  |invariant
    A universal path IS a path whose origin qualifier is universal — one concept; before [[DECISIONS#d11-universal-path|D11 universal-path]] it appeared at two ends (as a location kind here, as the origin trichotomy's third arm on path).
  |invariant
    This is the exact condition under which path, location, and identity safely interchange — the "Universal" presupposed by URI/URN/URL, explaining their conflation rather than observing it.
